### IPP-501 Quiz engine API tests
### How to use: run `npm run dev` in /server, then click "Send Request" above each request, top to bottom.

@baseUrl = http://localhost:5000/api

### Put real passwords only while testing, then put CHANGE_ME back
@adminEmail = raeeschechi302@gmail.com
@adminPassword = Change_me
@userEmail = arsalmustafa62+ipp2@gmail.com
@userPassword = secret456

### Picked up automatically
@userToken = {{userLogin.response.body.data.token}}
@adminToken = {{adminLogin.response.body.data.token}}
@sampleId = {{sampleQuiz.response.body.data.attemptId}}
@fullId = {{fullQuiz.response.body.data.attemptId}}
@q1 = {{fullQuiz.response.body.data.questions[0]._id}}
@q2 = {{fullQuiz.response.body.data.questions[1]._id}}
@q3 = {{fullQuiz.response.body.data.questions[2]._id}}
@s1 = {{sampleQuiz.response.body.data.questions[0]._id}}


### 1. Start WITHOUT login -> expect 401 "Please log in to continue"
POST {{baseUrl}}/quiz/start
Content-Type: application/json

{ "language": "php" }


### ---- Unpaid user: sample quiz ----

### 2. Login as unpaid user -> expect 200
# @name userLogin
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "{{userEmail}}", "password": "{{userPassword}}" }


### 3. Start -> expect 201 "Sample quiz started", "isSample": true, 5 questions, "timeLimit": 150
###    Check: questions have options but NO "correctOption" and NO "answer"
# @name sampleQuiz
POST {{baseUrl}}/quiz/start
Authorization: Bearer {{userToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "language": "php", "difficulty": "hard" }


### 4. Submit one answer (option 0) -> expect 200 "Quiz submitted", score 0 or 1 out of 5,
###    "review" shows correctOption + explanation for all 5
POST {{baseUrl}}/quiz/{{sampleId}}/submit
Authorization: Bearer {{userToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "answers": [
    { "question": "{{s1}}", "selectedOption": 0 }
  ]
}


### 5. Submit the same quiz again -> expect 409 "This quiz was already submitted"
POST {{baseUrl}}/quiz/{{sampleId}}/submit
Authorization: Bearer {{userToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "answers": [] }


### ---- Paid (admin has full access): full quiz ----

### 6. Admin login -> expect 200
# @name adminLogin
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "{{adminEmail}}", "password": "{{adminPassword}}" }


### 7. Start a full quiz -> expect 201 "Quiz started", "isSample": false, 6 questions, "timeLimit": 180
# @name fullQuiz
POST {{baseUrl}}/quiz/start
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "language": "php", "difficulty": "mixed" }


### 8. Only easy questions -> expect 6 questions, all "difficulty": "easy"
POST {{baseUrl}}/quiz/start
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "language": "php", "difficulty": "easy" }


### 9. Bad option -> expect 400 "selectedOption must be 0 to 3 or null"
POST {{baseUrl}}/quiz/{{fullId}}/submit
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "answers": [ { "question": "{{q1}}", "selectedOption": 7 } ] }


### 10. The unpaid user tries to submit the admin's quiz -> expect 404 "Quiz not found"
POST {{baseUrl}}/quiz/{{fullId}}/submit
Authorization: Bearer {{userToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "answers": [] }


### 11. Submit 3 answers (others count as skipped) -> expect 200, "total": 6, review for all 6,
###     "timeTaken" in seconds. Change the options to test right/wrong answers.
POST {{baseUrl}}/quiz/{{fullId}}/submit
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "answers": [
    { "question": "{{q1}}", "selectedOption": 0 },
    { "question": "{{q2}}", "selectedOption": 1 },
    { "question": "{{q3}}", "selectedOption": null }
  ]
}


### 12. Timer test: run request 7 again, WAIT more than 3 minutes 15 seconds, then send request 11
###     -> expect 200 "Time was up, so no answers were counted", score 0, "timedOut": true
